    "is the authoritative override consulted by khasi_engine/g2p.py BEFORE the",
    "rule engine runs.",
    "",
    "Sources (both Badaplin War 2001, Ki Sawa Bad Ki Dur Kyntien):",
    "  transcription_table  — Lynnong VI pp.55-56, the author's own per-word",
    "                         IPA (highest confidence; verbatim).",
    "  vowel_chart          — Lynnong V pp.52-54, the |aː| |ɛː| |ɔː| |aːi|",
    "                         |aːu| |ɔːi| long-vowel rows (word attested long;",
    "                         full IPA constructed by lengthening the g2p_v2",
    "                         nucleus — quality may be approximate).",
    "",
    "reason: length = phonemic long vowel; lexical_quality = irregular vowel",
    "quality the rules get wrong (leit, putharo).",
    "",
    "Extend this file as a native speaker / dictionary confirms more forms.",
    "Deliberately EXCLUDES length-ambiguous homographs (e.g. kam) that are",
    "short in one sense and long in another — g2p sees only the surface form",
    "and cannot disambiguate, so it must not guess."
